    "all::MayNov2020_P1HR__Q15__p15-15__m04__Circle-Theorems": {
      "status": "checked",
      "checkedBy": "Dr Eslam Ahmed + Codex",
      "updated": "2026-05-06T12:59:49",
      "topicNote": "Circle Theorems. The tag is correct.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "title": "Proof",
          "body": "By the alternate segment theorem, the angle between tangent \\(BC\\) and chord \\(BF\\) equals the angle in the opposite segment:\n\\[\n\\angle BEF=70^\\circ\n\\]\n\nGiven\n\\[\n\\angle EDF=40^\\circ\n\\]\n\nAngles \\(EDF\\) and \\(EBF\\) stand on the same chord \\(EF\\), so\n\\[\n\\angle EBF=40^\\circ\n\\]\n\nIn triangle \\(BEF\\),\n\\[\n\\angle EFB=180^\\circ-70^\\circ-40^\\circ=70^\\circ\n\\]\n\nSo\n\\[\n\\angle EFB=\\angle FBC=70^\\circ\n\\]\n\nThese are alternate interior angles, so\n\\[\nEF\\parallel ABC\n\\]"
        }
      ],
      "finalAnswer": "The tangent \\(ABC\\) is parallel to \\(EF\\)."
    },
